---@class posthog.messaging_suppressions.MessageSuppression
---@field id string Server-assigned UUID for this suppression entry.
---@field identifier string Normalized recipient email address. Suppression is keyed on this value, per team.
---@field source posthog.messaging_suppressions.SuppressionSourceEnum How the entry landed on the list: `BOUNCE` for automatic (bounce-driven), `COMPLAINT` for automatic (the recipient reported a message as spam), `MANUAL` for user-added via the UI/API. * `BOUNCE` - Bounce * `MANUAL` - Manual * `COMPLAINT` - Complaint
---@field reason string|distilled.Null Human-readable reason for the suppression (e.g. 'Auto-suppressed after 5 consecutive soft bounces').
---@field transient_bounce_count number Rolling count of consecutive soft bounces with no successful delivery in between. Reset to 0 on any successful delivery. Ignored for MANUAL entries.
---@field last_bounce_at string|distilled.Null Timestamp of the most recent bounce, if any.
---@field last_bounce_diagnostic string|distilled.Null SMTP diagnostic string from the most recent bounce (e.g. '550 5.1.1 user unknown'), kept for visibility.
---@field suppressed boolean Whether the address is actively suppressed. A BOUNCE row can exist while still only counting bounces (suppressed=false) before it crosses the threshold.
---@field suppressed_at string|distilled.Null Timestamp when the address was first suppressed.
---@field created_at string When the row was first created (first bounce or manual add).
---@field updated_at string When the row was last touched by any write.

